WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:16.575
When the boys returned in their pajamas, they all sang and danced.

2
00:00:16.576 --> 00:00:20.603
Soon their dancing turned into a noisy pillow fight.

3
00:00:20.604 --> 00:00:25.587
Wendy quieted them and told them it was time for a good-night story.

4
00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:31.757
She would tell them the story they loved best, but it was a story that Peter hated.

5
00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:38.268
Usually when she told this story, Peter would put his hands over his ears or leave the room.

6
00:00:38.269 --> 00:00:41.125
But tonight he remained on his stool.

7
00:00:41.126 --> 00:00:46.109
This story was closest to Wendy's heart, and it began like this:

8
00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:55.243
"Once upon a time, there was a man called Mr. Darling and he lived with a woman called Mrs. Darling."

9
00:00:55.244 --> 00:00:58.535
"I knew them," John interrupted.

10
00:00:58.536 --> 00:01:02.743
"I think I knew them too," Michael joined in.

11
00:01:02.744 --> 00:01:09.626
"They lived in a big house in London," Wendy continued, "and had three darling children.

12
00:01:09.627 --> 00:01:14.262
The children had a faithful nanny called Nana.

13
00:01:14.263 --> 00:01:21.090
But one evening, Mr. Darling was angry with Nana and chained her up in the yard.

14
00:01:21.091 --> 00:01:24.220
So the three children flew away."

15
00:01:24.221 --> 00:01:28.878
"This is a really good story," said Nibs.

16
00:01:28.879 --> 00:01:36.055
"They flew away to Neverland where the lost children live," continued Wendy.

17
00:01:36.056 --> 00:01:41.028
"That's us!" cried the Lost Boys, excited.

18
00:01:41.029 --> 00:01:50.337
"And was one of the lost children called Tootles?" asked Tootles, who already knew the story well.

19
00:01:50.338 --> 00:01:58.221
"Yes," replied Wendy. "But the parents were very sad that their children had flown away.

20
00:01:58.222 --> 00:02:04.302
And they visited the nursery every night waiting for their children to return."

21
00:02:04.303 --> 00:02:13.334
"This is a sad story. I don't see how it can have a happy ending," said Nibs, forgetting what followed.

22
00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:16.233
"Don't worry," said Wendy.

23
00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:26.237
"It turns out all right at the end because the children knew their mother would always leave the window open for them to fly back home.

24
00:02:26.238 --> 00:02:36.176
Mothers are loyal like that. And because the children knew this, they stayed away for a long time and had fun."

25
00:02:36.177 --> 00:02:41.862
"Did they ever go back home to their parents?" asked the boys.

26
00:02:41.863 --> 00:02:46.133
This was the part of the story that Peter really hated.

27
00:02:46.134 --> 00:02:54.326
"Yes. One day, they decided to fly back to the open nursery window," Wendy said.

28
00:02:54.327 --> 00:02:58.514
"Their mother and father greeted them with much love.

29
00:02:58.515 --> 00:03:02.037
They didn't even scold them for running away.

30
00:03:02.038 --> 00:03:07.876
And the whole family lived happily ever after."

31
00:03:07.877 --> 00:03:14.294
That was the story and everyone was very pleased with its ending—except for Peter.

32
00:03:14.295 --> 00:03:20.258
He hated grown-ups. He had his own story to tell about mothers.

33
00:03:20.259 --> 00:03:24.564
"Wendy, you are wrong about mothers," he said.

34
00:03:24.565 --> 00:03:30.917
And the boys gathered around him to hear his story—one that he had never told before.

35
00:03:30.918 --> 00:03:40.524
"Long ago," he told them, "I thought—like you, Wendy—that my mother would always keep the window open for me.

36
00:03:40.525 --> 00:03:44.527
So I stayed away for many moons and suns.

37
00:03:44.528 --> 00:03:48.399
Then I flew back, but the window was locked.

38
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.333
My mother had forgotten about me.

39
00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:55.875
And there was another little boy sleeping in my bed."

40
00:03:55.876 --> 00:04:02.578
This tale scared all the boys, especially John and Michael, who had been listening closely.

41
00:04:02.579 --> 00:04:08.760
The Lost Boys had been away from their mothers for a long time and so knew how to live without them.

42
00:04:08.761 --> 00:04:11.751
But John and Michael didn't know how.

43
00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:17.005
"Wendy, let's go home," they both cried.

44
00:04:17.006 --> 00:04:21.486
Wendy put her arms around them and thought about their request for a moment.

45
00:04:21.487 --> 00:04:27.805
"Yes," she said. "Maybe it is time to go home to our parents."

46
00:04:27.806 --> 00:04:30.955
The Lost Boys were shocked by this quick decision.

47
00:04:30.956 --> 00:04:35.221
"Tonight?" they asked, confused.

48
00:04:35.222 --> 00:04:38.692
"Yes, at once," Wendy replied.

49
00:04:38.693 --> 00:04:44.303
Suddenly an image of her mother crying in the empty nursery came to her mind.

50
00:04:44.304 --> 00:04:48.473
Peter, of course, refused to show his feelings to the group.

51
00:04:48.474 --> 00:04:57.261
Though he cared very much, he said coolly to Wendy, "If you wish, I'll make the necessary arrangements."

52
00:04:57.262 --> 00:05:05.360
But, in his heart of hearts, he wanted to cry.
